{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.HqBiFiltration","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.HqBiFiltration","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.HopfAlgebra.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HqBiFiltration.figure_eight_instance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HqBiFiltration.figure_eight_instance","kind":"def","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hq-bi-filtration.lean#L92-L100","doc":"The figure-8 instance: the self-conjugate `(2, 2)` cell of\n`H_4(q)` admits a non-empty depth-2 bi-filtration stratum,\nrealised numerically by `Vol(4_1) = 2 Cl_2(π/3)` at 50 dps.\nPer Gemini PR #634 review: replaces vacuous `True` with the\n`Nonempty (BiFiltration q 2 [2, 2])` claim. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HqBiFiltration.bar_compatible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HqBiFiltration.bar_compatible","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hq-bi-filtration.lean#L76-L87","doc":"Compatibility with bar involution: every bi-filtration element\nat stratum `(n, lam)` has a mirror at stratum `(n, lam.transpose)`\nvia the bar involution.  The transpose function on partitions\nis computed concretely below.  Per Gemini PR #634 review:\nreplaces vacuous `True` with a quantified statement asserting\nnon-emptiness of the mirror stratum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HqBiFiltration.convolution_compatible","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HqBiFiltration.convolution_compatible","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hq-bi-filtration.lean#L52-L74","doc":"Compatibility with convolution: every pair of bi-filtration\nelements at strata `(n₁, lam₁)` and `(n₂, lam₂)` lifts to *some*\nelement of the sum-degree stratum `(n₁ + n₂, lam')` for an\nappropriate cell-merging `lam'`.  Concrete schematic statement\nusing the opaque `BiFiltration` type; full version with\nexplicit `lam'` requires non-opaque `BiFiltration` per\n`def:hq-bi-filtration`'s closure-properties table.\n\nPer Gemini PR #634 review: replaces the previous vacuous\n`True` placeholder with a quantified statement over actual\n`BiFiltration` types. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HqBiFiltration.BiFiltration","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HqBiFiltration.BiFiltration","kind":"opaque","line":42,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hq-bi-filtration.lean#L42-L50","doc":"**Definition (`def:hq-bi-filtration`).** The knot-indexed\nbi-filtration of `H_q`:\n\n  `H_q^{(n, K)}` := grouplikes at depth `n` localised on the\n  `λ_K`-Wedderburn block.\n\nTwo-axis grading: depth `n` (Goncharov side) × knot index\n`K` (Hecke cell side). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:hq-bi-filtration","label":"def:hq-bi-filtration","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hq-bi-filtration.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HqBiFiltration.CentralIdempotent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HqBiFiltration.CentralIdempotent","kind":"opaque","line":36,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hq-bi-filtration.lean#L36-L40","doc":"Central primitive idempotent `e_{λ_K}` for a partition\n`λ_K ⊢ n_K` (the dominant Wedderburn cell of the Hecke\nalgebra `H_{n_K}(q)` for knot/braid class `K`). Wired through\n`prop:explicit-central-idempotent`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HqBiFiltration.GroupLikeDepth","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HqBiFiltration.GroupLikeDepth","kind":"opaque","line":32,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hq-bi-filtration.lean#L32-L34","doc":"Iterated-integral depth filtration `G^{(n)}(H_q)` on grouplikes\nof `H_q`. Wired through `conj:gb-depth-period-correspondence`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HqBiFiltration.ConvolutionHopfAlgebra","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.HqBiFiltration.ConvolutionHopfAlgebra","kind":"opaque","line":28,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/hq-bi-filtration.lean#L28-L30","doc":"The substrate convolution Hopf algebra `H_q`. Placeholder;\nwired through `def:frobenius-hopf-substrate`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}